-- src:6927 | A financial year of the company beginning—(a) on or after 17 June 1994, and(b) before 17 June 2003 | The last financial year of the company to begin before 17 June 2023.
-- src:6928 | A financial year of the company beginning—(a) on or after 17 June 2003, and(b) before 17 June 2016 | No qualifying selection procedureWhere neither the first financial year of the maximum engagement period nor any subsequent financial year is one for which the auditor has been appointed following the carrying out of a qualifying selection procedure, the later of-(a) the last financial year of the company to begin before 17 June 2016, and(b) the last financial year of the company to begin within the period of 10 years beginning with the first day of the first financial year of the maximum engagement period.No qualifying selection procedure within 10 yearsWhere the last day of the last financial year of the company to begin within the period of 10 years beginning with the first day of the last financial year of the company for which the auditor was appointed following a qualifying selection procedure is before 17 June 2016—(a) the last financial year of the company to begin before 17 June 2016, unless(b) the auditor is appointed following a qualifying selection procedure for the first financial year of the company to begin on or after 17 June 2016, in which case it is the last financial year of the company to begin within the period of 20 years beginning with the first day of the first financial year of the maximum engagement period.Qualifying selection procedure within 10 yearsIn any other case, the earlier of-(a) the last financial year of the company to begin within the period of 10 years beginning with the first day of the last financial year of the company for which the auditor was appointed following a qualifying selection procedure, and(b) the last financial year of the company to begin within the period of 20 years beginning with the first day of the first financial year of the maximum engagement period.
-- src:6929 | A financial year of the company beginning on or after 17 June 2016 | The earlier of—(a) the last financial year of the company to begin within the period of 10 years beginning with the first day of the last financial year of the company for which the auditor was appointed following a qualifying selection procedure, and(b) the last financial year of the company to begin within the period of 20 years beginning with the first day of the first financial year of the maximum engagement period.
@ref s 494ZA(1) The maximum engagement period and the Table (src:6922-6929)
GIVEN years IS A LIST OF `s 494ZA financial year`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 494ZA financial year`
`s 494ZA(1) the last financial year of the maximum engagement period` MEANS
    CONSIDER years
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no financial year is supplied
    WHEN firstYear FOLLOWED BY rest THEN `s 494ZA(1) the Table applied to the first financial year` firstYear years

-- src:6922 | (1) Where a person is auditor of a company for consecutive financial years, the maximum engagement period of the person as auditor of the company—
-- src:6923 | (a) begins with the first of those years (see the appropriate entry in the first column of the following Table), and
-- src:6924 | (b) ends with the financial year specified in the corresponding entry in the second column of the Table:
-- src:6925 | First financial year of the maximum engagement period | Last financial year of the maximum engagement period
-- src:6926 | A financial year of the company beginning before 17 June 1994 | The last financial year of the company to begin before 17 June 2020.
-- src:6927 | A financial year of the company beginning—(a) on or after 17 June 1994, and(b) before 17 June 2003 | The last financial year of the company to begin before 17 June 2023.
-- src:6928 | A financial year of the company beginning—(a) on or after 17 June 2003, and(b) before 17 June 2016 | No qualifying selection procedureWhere neither the first financial year of the maximum engagement period nor any subsequent financial year is one for which the auditor has been appointed following the carrying out of a qualifying selection procedure, the later of-(a) the last financial year of the company to begin before 17 June 2016, and(b) the last financial year of the company to begin within the period of 10 years beginning with the first day of the first financial year of the maximum engagement period.No qualifying selection procedure within 10 yearsWhere the last day of the last financial year of the company to begin within the period of 10 years beginning with the first day of the last financial year of the company for which the auditor was appointed following a qualifying selection procedure is before 17 June 2016—(a) the last financial year of the company to begin before 17 June 2016, unless(b) the auditor is appointed following a qualifying selection procedure for the first financial year of the company to begin on or after 17 June 2016, in which case it is the last financial year of the company to begin within the period of 20 years beginning with the first day of the first financial year of the maximum engagement period.Qualifying selection procedure within 10 yearsIn any other case, the earlier of-(a) the last financial year of the company to begin within the period of 10 years beginning with the first day of the last financial year of the company for which the auditor was appointed following a qualifying selection procedure, and(b) the last financial year of the company to begin within the period of 20 years beginning with the first day of the first financial year of the maximum engagement period.
-- src:6929 | A financial year of the company beginning on or after 17 June 2016 | The earlier of—(a) the last financial year of the company to begin within the period of 10 years beginning with the first day of the last financial year of the company for which the auditor was appointed following a qualifying selection procedure, and(b) the last financial year of the company to begin within the period of 20 years beginning with the first day of the first financial year of the maximum engagement period.
@ref s 494ZA(1) The Table: the second column for the first financial year of the maximum engagement period (src:6922-6929)
GIVEN `the first financial year of the maximum engagement period` IS A `s 494ZA financial year`
      years IS A LIST OF `s 494ZA financial year`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 494ZA financial year`
`s 494ZA(1) the Table applied to the first financial year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- row 1: a financial year of the company beginning before 17 June 1994
        IF first LESS THAN Date 17 6 1994
        THEN `s 494ZA the last financial year of the company to begin before the day` (Date 17 6 2020) years
        -- row 2: beginning on or after 17 June 1994 and before 17 June 2003
        IF first LESS THAN Date 17 6 2003
        THEN `s 494ZA the last financial year of the company to begin before the day` (Date 17 6 2023) years
        -- row 3: beginning on or after 17 June 2003 and before 17 June 2016
        IF first LESS THAN Date 17 6 2016
        THEN row3
        -- row 4: beginning on or after 17 June 2016
        OTHERWISE earlierOfTheLimits
    WHERE
        first MEANS `the first financial year of the maximum engagement period`'s `s 494ZA first day of the financial year`
        qspYears MEANS filter (GIVEN year YIELD year's `s 494ZA the auditor was appointed for the year following a qualifying selection procedure`) years
        lastQspYear MEANS `s 494ZA the last one of the years` qspYears
        -- the last year, beginning before 17 June 2016, for which the auditor was appointed following a qualifying selection procedure (fork F20)
        lastQspYearBefore2016 MEANS `s 494ZA the last one of the years` (filter (GIVEN year YIELD year's `s 494ZA first day of the financial year` LESS THAN Date 17 6 2016) qspYears)
        row3 MEANS
            BRANCH
                -- "No qualifying selection procedure": neither the first financial year nor any subsequent year is one for which the auditor was appointed following a qualifying selection procedure
                IF NOT (any (GIVEN year YIELD year's `s 494ZA the auditor was appointed for the year following a qualifying selection procedure`) years)
                THEN `s 494ZA the later of the two years` (`s 494ZA the last financial year of the company to begin before the day` (Date 17 6 2016) years) (`s 494ZA the last financial year of the company to begin within the period of years beginning with the day` first 10 years)
                -- "No qualifying selection procedure within 10 years": the 10 years from the last such year (before 17 June 2016) end before 17 June 2016
                IF noQspWithin10Years EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN row3Case2
                IF noQspWithin10Years EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the years supplied do not reach the end of the 10 years
                -- "Qualifying selection procedure within 10 years": in any other case
                OTHERWISE earlierOfTheLimits
        -- the last day of the last financial year to begin within the 10 years beginning with the first day of the last qualifying year is before 17 June 2016
        noQspWithin10Years MEANS
            CONSIDER lastQspYearBefore2016
            WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- internal flag, not an answer: no qualifying selection procedure before 17 June 2016, so the 10 years run from a later year and do not end before 17 June 2016 (sub-case (ii) does not arise; fork F20)
            WHEN JUST qspYear THEN
                CONSIDER `s 494ZA the last financial year of the company to begin within the period of years beginning with the day` (qspYear's `s 494ZA first day of the financial year`) 10 years
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): internal flag; the years supplied do not reach the end of the 10 years
                WHEN JUST lastWithin THEN JUST (lastWithin's `s 494ZA last day of the financial year` LESS THAN Date 17 6 2016)
        row3Case2 MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 494ZA the first financial year of the company to begin on or after the day` (Date 17 6 2016) years
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the years supplied do not reach the first financial year to begin on or after 17 June 2016
            WHEN JUST post2016 THEN
                -- "(a) the last financial year of the company to begin before 17 June 2016, unless (b) the auditor is appointed following a qualifying selection procedure for the first financial year of the company to begin on or after 17 June 2016, in which case it is the last financial year of the company to begin within the period of 20 years beginning with the first day of the first financial year of the maximum engagement period"
                IF post2016's `s 494ZA the auditor was appointed for the year following a qualifying selection procedure`
                THEN `s 494ZA the last financial year of the company to begin within the period of years beginning with the day` first 20 years
                ELSE `s 494ZA the last financial year of the company to begin before the day` (Date 17 6 2016) years
        earlierOfTheLimits MEANS
            CONSIDER lastQspYear
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Table asks for "the last financial year of the company for which the auditor was appointed following a qualifying selection procedure" and none is supplied
            WHEN JUST qspYear THEN
                `s 494ZA the earlier of the two years` (`s 494ZA the last financial year of the company to begin within the period of years beginning with the day` (qspYear's `s 494ZA first day of the financial year`) 10 years) (`s 494ZA the last financial year of the company to begin within the period of years beginning with the day` first 20 years)

-- src:6930 | (2) Where the first financial year of the maximum engagement period begins on or after 17 June 2003, the maximum engagement period may be extended by a period of no more than 2 years with the approval of the competent authority.
@ref s 494ZA(2) The maximum engagement period may be extended (src:6930-6930)
GIVEN `the first day of the first financial year of the maximum engagement period` IS A DATE
      `the length of the proposed extension, in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the competent authority has approved the extension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 494ZA(3) the competent authority may give its approval` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 494ZA(2) the maximum engagement period may be extended by the period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the first day of the first financial year of the maximum engagement period` LESS THAN Date 17 6 2003
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the first financial year of the maximum engagement period begins on or after 17 June 2003"
        IF `the length of the proposed extension, in years` GREATER THAN 2
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be extended by a period of no more than 2 years"
        IF (NOT `the competent authority has approved the extension`) OR `s 494ZA(3) the competent authority may give its approval` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "with the approval of the competent authority" (fork F22)
        IF `s 494ZA(3) the competent authority may give its approval` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the competent authority may give its approval is not known

-- src:6930 | (2) Where the first financial year of the maximum engagement period begins on or after 17 June 2003, the maximum engagement period may be extended by a period of no more than 2 years with the approval of the competent authority.
@ref s 494ZA(2) The extension of the end of the period (src:6930-6930)
GIVEN `the last day of the last financial year of the maximum engagement period` IS A DATE
      `the length of the extension, in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 494ZA(2) the last day of the maximum engagement period as extended` MEANS
    `add years` `the last day of the last financial year of the maximum engagement period` `the length of the extension, in years` -- "extended by a period of no more than 2 years": the end moves later by the approved period (fork F23)

-- src:6931 | (3) Such approval may be given by the competent authority only if it is satisfied that exceptional circumstances exist.
@ref s 494ZA(3) Approval only if satisfied that exceptional circumstances exist (src:6931-6931)
GIVEN `the competent authority is satisfied that exceptional circumstances exist` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 494ZA(3) the competent authority may give its approval` MEANS
    IF `the competent authority is satisfied that exceptional circumstances exist`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Such approval may be given by the competent authority only if it is satisfied that exceptional circumstances exist"

-- src:6932 | (4) Where the competent authority gives its approval as mentioned in subsection (2)—
-- src:6933 | (a) the second column of the Table in subsection (1) has effect with the necessary modifications, and
@ref s 494ZA(4)(a) The second column of the Table has effect with the necessary modifications (src:6932-6933)
GIVEN `the competent authority has given its approval as mentioned in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 494ZA(4)(a) the second column of the Table has effect with the necessary modifications` MEANS
    IF `the competent authority has given its approval as mentioned in subsection (2)`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "the necessary modifications" are not spelled out; the extension itself is encoded as the end of the period moved later (section 494ZA(2))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the competent authority gives its approval as mentioned in subsection (2)": no approval, no modification

-- src:6932 | (4) Where the competent authority gives its approval as mentioned in subsection (2)—
@ref s 494ZA(4) (src:6932-6932)
-- src:6934 | (b) the first appointment to be made after the end of the period as so extended must be made following a qualifying selection procedure.
@ref s 494ZA(4)(b) The first appointment after the extended period must follow a qualifying selection procedure (src:6934-6934)
GIVEN `the competent authority has given its approval as mentioned in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is the first appointment to be made after the end of the period as so extended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is made following a qualifying selection procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 494ZA(4)(b) the appointment meets the requirement of a qualifying selection procedure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the competent authority has given its approval as mentioned in subsection (2)`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the competent authority gives its approval as mentioned in subsection (2)"
        IF NOT `the appointment is the first appointment to be made after the end of the period as so extended`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the first appointment to be made after the end of the period as so extended"
        IF `the appointment is made following a qualifying selection procedure`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the first appointment to be made after the end of the period as so extended must be made following a qualifying selection procedure" (a bare must not done: fork F4)

-- src:6935 | (5) In this section “qualifying selection procedure” means—
-- src:6936 | (a) in the case of an appointment for a financial year beginning on or after 17 June 2016 made after the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2017 come into force—
-- src:6937 | (i) if the company is a private company and has an audit committee, a selection procedure that complies with the requirements of section 485A(4) and (5)(a) and (b),
-- src:6938 | (ii) if the company is a public company and has an audit committee, a selection procedure that complies with the requirements of subsections 489A(4) and (5)(a) and(b), ...
-- src:6939 | (iii) if the company is a private company and does not have an audit committee, a selection procedure that complies with the requirements of section 485B(4),
-- src:6940 | (iv) if the company is a public company and does not have an audit committee, a selection procedure that complies with the requirements of section 489B(4),
-- src:6941 | (b) in any other case, a selection procedure that substantially meets the requirements of Article 16(2) to (5) of the Audit Regulation as it had effect immediately before IP completion day, having regard to the circumstances at the time (including whether the company had an audit committee).
@ref s 494ZA(5) "qualifying selection procedure" (src:6935-6941)
DECLARE `s 494ZA(5) compliance of the selection procedure` HAS
    `s 494ZA(5)(a)(i) the procedure complies with the requirements of section 485A(4) and (5)(a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 494ZA(5)(a)(ii) the procedure complies with the requirements of subsections 489A(4) and (5)(a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 494ZA(5)(a)(iii) the procedure complies with the requirements of section 485B(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 494ZA(5)(a)(iv) the procedure complies with the requirements of section 489B(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 494ZA(5)(b) the procedure substantially meets the requirements of Article 16(2) to (5) of the Audit Regulation as it had effect immediately before IP completion day, having regard to the circumstances at the time` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:6935 | (5) In this section “qualifying selection procedure” means—
-- src:6936 | (a) in the case of an appointment for a financial year beginning on or after 17 June 2016 made after the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2017 come into force—
-- src:6937 | (i) if the company is a private company and has an audit committee, a selection procedure that complies with the requirements of section 485A(4) and (5)(a) and (b),
-- src:6938 | (ii) if the company is a public company and has an audit committee, a selection procedure that complies with the requirements of subsections 489A(4) and (5)(a) and(b), ...
-- src:6939 | (iii) if the company is a private company and does not have an audit committee, a selection procedure that complies with the requirements of section 485B(4),
-- src:6940 | (iv) if the company is a public company and does not have an audit committee, a selection procedure that complies with the requirements of section 489B(4),
-- src:6941 | (b) in any other case, a selection procedure that substantially meets the requirements of Article 16(2) to (5) of the Audit Regulation as it had effect immediately before IP completion day, having regard to the circumstances at the time (including whether the company had an audit committee).
@ref s 494ZA(5) "qualifying selection procedure" (src:6935-6941)
GIVEN `the first day of the financial year for which the appointment is made` IS A DATE
      `the appointment is made after the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2017 come into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has an audit committee` IS A BOOLEAN
      compliance IS A `s 494ZA(5) compliance of the selection procedure`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 494ZA(5) the selection procedure is a qualifying selection procedure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF from2016 AND `the company is a private company` AND `the company has an audit committee`
        THEN IF compliance's `s 494ZA(5)(a)(i) the procedure complies with the requirements of section 485A(4) and (5)(a) and (b)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“qualifying selection procedure” means— (a) ... (i) if the company is a private company and has an audit committee, a selection procedure that complies with the requirements of section 485A(4) and (5)(a) and (b)"
        IF from2016 AND (`the company is a private company`) AND (NOT `the company has an audit committee`)
        THEN IF compliance's `s 494ZA(5)(a)(iii) the procedure complies with the requirements of section 485B(4)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(iii) if the company is a private company and does not have an audit committee, a selection procedure that complies with the requirements of section 485B(4)"
        IF from2016 AND (NOT `the company is a private company`) AND `the company has an audit committee`
        THEN IF compliance's `s 494ZA(5)(a)(ii) the procedure complies with the requirements of subsections 489A(4) and (5)(a) and (b)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) if the company is a public company and has an audit committee, a selection procedure that complies with the requirements of subsections 489A(4) and (5)(a) and (b)"
        IF from2016 AND (NOT `the company is a private company`) AND (NOT `the company has an audit committee`)
        THEN IF compliance's `s 494ZA(5)(a)(iv) the procedure complies with the requirements of section 489B(4)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(iv) if the company is a public company and does not have an audit committee, a selection procedure that complies with the requirements of section 489B(4)"
        OTHERWISE IF compliance's `s 494ZA(5)(b) the procedure substantially meets the requirements of Article 16(2) to (5) of the Audit Regulation as it had effect immediately before IP completion day, having regard to the circumstances at the time` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in any other case, a selection procedure that substantially meets the requirements of Article 16(2) to (5) of the Audit Regulation as it had effect immediately before IP completion day, having regard to the circumstances at the time (including whether the company had an audit committee)"
    WHERE
        -- (a) "in the case of an appointment for a financial year beginning on or after 17 June 2016 made after the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2017 come into force"
        from2016 MEANS `the first day of the financial year for which the appointment is made` AT LEAST Date 17 6 2016 AND `the appointment is made after the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2017 come into force`

§§ `s 494A Interpretation`

-- The text shows omitted words as "..." after the definition of "audit committee" (raw line 6950) and twice after paragraph (c) of the
-- definition of "public interest entity" (raw lines 6968 and 6969): coverage rows "repealed or blank"; finding 2 and fork F21.

-- src:6944 | “audit committee” means a body which performs—
-- src:6945 | (a) the functions referred to in—
-- src:6946 | (i) rule 7.1.3 of the Disclosure Guidance and Transparency Rules sourcebook made by the Financial Conduct Authority (audit committees and their functions) under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000, or
-- src:6947 | (ii) rule 2.4 of the Audit Committee Part of the Rulebook made by the Prudential Regulation Authority (audit committee) under that Act,
-- src:6948 | as they have effect on IP completion day, or
-- src:6949 | (b) equivalent functions.
@ref s 494A "audit committee" (src:6944-6949)
GIVEN `the body performs the functions referred to in rule 7.1.3 of the Disclosure Guidance and Transparency Rules sourcebook made by the Financial Conduct Authority (audit committees and their functions), as they have effect on IP completion day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body performs the functions referred to in rule 2.4 of the Audit Committee Part of the Rulebook made by the Prudential Regulation Authority (audit committee), as they have effect on IP completion day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body performs equivalent functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 494A "audit committee" the body is an audit committee` MEANS
    IF    `the body performs the functions referred to in rule 7.1.3 of the Disclosure Guidance and Transparency Rules sourcebook made by the Financial Conduct Authority (audit committees and their functions), as they have effect on IP completion day`
       OR `the body performs the functions referred to in rule 2.4 of the Audit Committee Part of the Rulebook made by the Prudential Regulation Authority (audit committee), as they have effect on IP completion day`
       OR `the body performs equivalent functions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“audit committee” means a body which performs— (a) the functions referred to in— (i) rule 7.1.3 ..., or (ii) rule 2.4 ..., as they have effect on IP completion day, or (b) equivalent functions" (fork F21 on the omitted words that follow)

-- src:6951 | “Auditor General” means—
-- src:6952 | (a) the Comptroller and Auditor General,
-- src:6953 | (b) the Auditor General for Scotland,
-- src:6954 | (c) the Auditor General for Wales, or
-- src:6955 | (d) the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland;
@ref s 494A "Auditor General" (src:6951-6955)
GIVEN `the person is the Comptroller and Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Auditor General for Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Auditor General for Wales` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 494A "Auditor General" the person is an Auditor General` MEANS
    IF    `the person is the Comptroller and Auditor General` OR `the person is the Auditor General for Scotland`
       OR `the person is the Auditor General for Wales` OR `the person is the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Auditor General” means— (a) the Comptroller and Auditor General, (b) the Auditor General for Scotland, (c) the Auditor General for Wales, or (d) the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland"

-- src:6956 | “issuer” has the same meaning as in Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (see section 102A(6));
@ref s 494A "issuer" (src:6956-6956)
GIVEN `the person is an issuer within the meaning of Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (see section 102A(6))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 494A "issuer" the person is an issuer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person is an issuer within the meaning of Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (see section 102A(6))`
    WHEN JUST answer THEN JUST answer -- the borrowed definition's own answer (JUST FALSE is the other Act's no, supplied as an input)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "has the same meaning as in Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000", which is not among the sources

-- src:6957 | “network” means an association of persons other than a firm co-operating in audit work by way of—
-- src:6958 | (a) profit-sharing;
-- src:6959 | (b) cost sharing;
-- src:6960 | (c) common ownership, control or management;
-- src:6961 | (d) common quality control policies and procedures;
-- src:6962 | (e) common business strategy; or
-- src:6963 | (f) use of a common name;
@ref s 494A "network" (src:6957-6963)
GIVEN `the persons form an association of persons other than a firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they co-operate in audit work by way of profit-sharing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they co-operate in audit work by way of cost sharing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they co-operate in audit work by way of common ownership, control or management` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they co-operate in audit work by way of common quality control policies and procedures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they co-operate in audit work by way of common business strategy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they co-operate in audit work by way of use of a common name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 494A "network" the association is a network` MEANS
    IF    `the persons form an association of persons other than a firm`
      AND (    `they co-operate in audit work by way of profit-sharing`
            OR `they co-operate in audit work by way of cost sharing`
            OR `they co-operate in audit work by way of common ownership, control or management`
            OR `they co-operate in audit work by way of common quality control policies and procedures`
            OR `they co-operate in audit work by way of common business strategy`
            OR `they co-operate in audit work by way of use of a common name`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“network” means an association of persons other than a firm co-operating in audit work by way of— (a) profit-sharing; (b) cost sharing; (c) common ownership, control or management; (d) common quality control policies and procedures; (e) common business strategy; or (f) use of a common name"

-- src:6964 | “public interest entity ” means—
-- src:6965 | (a) an issuer whose transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market;
-- src:6966 | (b) a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013 of the European Parliament and of the Council, which is a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation;
-- src:6967 | (c) a person who would be an insurance undertaking as defined in Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC of 19 December 1991 of the European Parliament and of the Council on the annual accounts and consolidated accounts of insurance undertakings as that Article had effect immediately before IP completion day, were the United Kingdom a member State;
@ref s 494A "public interest entity" (src:6964-6967)
GIVEN `s 494A "issuer" the entity is an issuer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `its transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013 which is a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the entity would be an insurance undertaking as defined in Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC as that Article had effect immediately before IP completion day, were the United Kingdom a member State` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 494A "public interest entity" the entity is a public interest entity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF    (`s 494A "issuer" the entity is an issuer` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `its transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market`)
           OR `the entity is a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013 which is a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `the entity would be an insurance undertaking as defined in Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC as that Article had effect immediately before IP completion day, were the United Kingdom a member State` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF    (`s 494A "issuer" the entity is an issuer` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR (NOT `its transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market`))
          AND `the entity is a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013 which is a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
          AND `the entity would be an insurance undertaking as defined in Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC as that Article had effect immediately before IP completion day, were the United Kingdom a member State` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“public interest entity” means— (a) an issuer whose transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market; (b) a credit institution ... which is a CRR firm ...; (c) a person who would be an insurance undertaking ..." (fork F21 on the omitted words that follow)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a borrowed definition ("issuer": Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000; Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013; Council Directive 91/674/EEC) is not known
